apply."],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","class":"primary wide"},"Apply land commission"],["P",{"class":"field-help"},"The allowance limits total future spending; it is not taken from the treasury in advance. Each order must leave the chosen treasury reserve. Other realm orders can still spend that reserve. Commissions share the treasury in stable hearth order."],["P",{"class":"field-help"},"Only unimproved, worked land is considered. A resource deposit accepts only its matching extraction site. Existing sites are kept; commissions do not claim land, cultivate biomes or assign workers."],["P",{"class":"field-help"},"Siege and occupation pause work. Ending a commission keeps paid work underway. Building, cultivating or cancelling land work yourself ends the commission after a successful order. Losing the hearth ends it; cancelled work is not refunded."]],["DETAILS",{"class":"land-options","data-testid":"settlement-road"},["SUMMARY",{},"Road connections"],["P",{"class":"field-help"},"Settlements gradually connect to an older town along a charted land route. Workers survey one town per realm each turn. Completed roads cross forest and hills for 1 movement point and remain after conquest."],["P",{},"Explore toward another owned settlement to establish a connection. Water and mountains require another route."]],["P",{"class":"land-stage","data-testid":"settlement-stage"},"colony"," · Capital"],["P",{"class":"field-help"},"Colony: 1–2 people · Settlement: 3–7 · City: 8+. Capital is a separate designation."],["P",{"data-testid":"land-counts"},"21"," claimed tiles · ","0"," / ","1"," assigned workers · reach ","16"],["P",{"class":"field-help"},"Connected territory and population can keep growing. Each person can work one additional tile. Larger hearths need more food, investment and civic upkeep."],["P",{"class":"field-help","data-testid":"hearth-growth-economy"},"Next person: ","0"," / ","12"," food · consumption ","2"," food per turn · civic upkeep ","2"," coin (","1"," popula